From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:20:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 120/148] [ae-patch] Put the model grid's check before the name
 so it marks the right model

In the composer menu's two-column model grid the check sat at each cell's
right edge, beside the next column's model, so a session on Opus showed the
check next to Haiku. The grid's items now pad on the left and draw the check
there. Important modifiers, since the composer menu's own CSS sets item
padding.
---
 web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx b/web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx
index 0ad7a6b4ca36e1be179f586d497565e82ad11db3..85d5adfcd014d7cca724d6c878c96e3f832b336c 100644
--- a/web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx
+++ b/web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx
@@ -4625,7 +4625,12 @@ function CompactConfigChoice({ choice }: { choice: ComposerConfigChoice }) {
       onSelect={(event) => event.preventDefault()}
       onCheckedChange={choice.onSelect}
       data-testid={choice.testId}
-      className={cn("min-h-8 whitespace-normal break-words", choice.className)}
+      // In the two-column grid a right-edge check sits beside the next column's
+      // model and reads as its; the check goes before the name instead.
+      className={cn(
+        "min-h-8 pr-2! pl-7! whitespace-normal break-words [&>[data-slot=dropdown-menu-checkbox-item-indicator]]:right-auto [&>[data-slot=dropdown-menu-checkbox-item-indicator]]:left-1.5",
+        choice.className,
+      )}
       {...choice.data}
     >
       {choice.label}
